      "writtenOn": "2021-08-19T15:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that most of the awkwardness can be chalked up to the naming of child variables.\n\nI do wonder about the use of \"uniform\" for a thing that is used like a function. Samplers are uniforms in GLSL, but they encapsulate things that are unchanging for a draw (a texture and the sample parameters used with it) and past as arguments to functions that return a non-uniform result.",
      "parentUuid": "dbc7485d_70a750c1",
      "revId": "7c934cb85d8787a83424f9285bbf3d18d969c82e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
